name advdate
category Package
revision 20538
shortdesc Print a date relative to "today"
relocated 1
longdesc Provides macros which can add a specified number of days to the
longdesc current date (as specified in \today), to save, set and restore
longdesc the 'current date' and to print it. Intended use is, for
longdesc example, in invoices "payable within 14 days from today", etc.
longdesc The package has only been tested with Czech dates.
runfiles size=2
 RELOC/tex/latex/advdate/advdate.sty
catalogue-ctan /macros/latex/contrib/advdate
catalogue-license lppl1.3
catalogue-topics date-time

name advice
category Package
revision 69283
shortdesc Extend commands and environments
relocated 1
longdesc Like its namesake from the Emacs world, this cross-format
longdesc package implements a generic framework for extending the
longdesc functionality of selected commands and environments. It was
longdesc developed as an auxiliary package of Memoize. This is why it
longdesc is, somewhat unconventionally, documented alongside that
longdesc package. This applies to both the manual and the documented
longdesc code listing.
