revision 37659
shortdesc "Controls in Contents" for the cyber package
relocated 1
longdesc This package is used in concert with the cyber package to make
longdesc documents with annotations of compliance with cybersecurity
longdesc requirements. "cic" stands for "Controls in Contents", and when
longdesc you include this package, some notations of compliance are
longdesc added to section names as seen in the table of contents of the
longdesc final document. It also makes your document more brittle in
longdesc unexpected ways: for example, when you use cybercic in the same
longdesc document as hyperref, you cannot use any formatting in your
longdesc section titles. So don't use cybercic unless you need to.
