longdesc versions of a LaTeX document. The command \version prints the
longdesc version and build numbers; each time you compile your document,
longdesc the build number is increased by one. By placing \version in
longdesc the header or footer, each page can be marked with the unique
longdesc build number describing the progress of your document.
